#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115096 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115267 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e509fc70-f78c-5daa-bf55-e23ed6a2b046" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Graph of an Elementary Cubic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "4868c33a-6977-573e-ad7a-bd219fa3a200" :question/math-academy-id "e-5046" :question/problem "Which of the following plots is the graph of $y = -x^3?$\n\n![](images/ba/babbe4306b4a068c96f9dc820af3b02a6e25d5779928108f3d783dc0684fdf27.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that for $x>0,$ the graph of $y=-x^3$ decreases very rapidly as we increase $x.$ We say that $y \\rightarrow -\\infty$ as $x \\rightarrow \\infty.$ The only graphs that exhibit this decreasing property are III and IV.\n\nNow, we need to choose between graphs III and IV. To do this, let's evaluate $y=-x^3$ at some value of $x,$ say $x=1.$ Substituting $x=1$ into the function, we get\n\n$$\ny = -(1)^3 = -1,\n$$\n\nso the correct graph must pass through the point $(1,-1).$ Only graph III satisfies this criterion.\n\nTherefore, graph III corresponds to the graph of $y=-x^3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115097 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40093136-bd98-5ca4-838e-58e47b317950" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Vertical Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "16ea2f1f-3e5e-547d-8172-02fbe49c2ce7" :question/math-academy-id "e-5047" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y=x^3+2.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have $y=x^3{\\color{blue}\\,+\\,2},$ we need to translate the graph of $y=x^3$ *up* by $\\color{blue}2$ units. \n\nSo, the graph of $y=x^3+2$ looks as follows:\n\n![](images/54/54030b86feaed3fd9b3e818654dae831f4456159d6ae32f5e3619b6f0e1369a7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115098 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8acb08f-56b0-5a1b-b503-ba70e1cf88e6" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Horizontal Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "59505e8f-fe13-5096-9186-b1ea1a095432" :question/math-academy-id "e-5048" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y=(x-2)^3.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have $\\color{blue}-2$ inside the brackets, we translate the graph of $y=x^3$ by $\\color{blue}2$ units to the *right*. \n\nSo, the graph of $y=(x-2)^3$ looks as follows:\n\n![](images/82/82978268bdfe405201f3b5e3e8927c81c3379bcf2933a34e15b6ba304cbd770d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115099 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f1cf641-888f-576c-b9c3-0bdf62a00fb8" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Horizontal and Vertical Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "07f7ddf8-109e-5cc4-b089-16e03f3f2915" :question/math-academy-id "e-5054" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $y=-(x+1)^3-3.$" :question/worked-solution "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=-x^3$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $\\color{red}+1$ inside the parentheses means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *left*, and\n\n- the $\\color{blue}-3$ outside the parentheses means a vertical translation of $3$ units *down*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/b5/b5f3fac4f76321abdd825c6e7d5ab5b60916149bbffc7a94a8bd3e932c17d8ea.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115267 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e509fc70-f78c-5daa-bf55-e23ed6a2b046" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Graph of an Elementary Cubic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33fea308-610c-5421-ab79-bb3a1649e672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526602} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce8035c-cf2a-5f2a-b299-14745d4be4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526717} {:answer/id #uuid "7670b248-dbe6-5812-a098-f64191a82dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526736} {:answer/id #uuid "82ee4a4f-63b3-5299-b797-c0c7b0604298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526766} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f3a87e-a8b6-506d-a966-786618c6b1cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82ee4a4f-63b3-5299-b797-c0c7b0604298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526766} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1a37a95-3f08-5505-9824-80e83cc36021" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4aa71abb-1f45-5c68-95b9-e97d2bf13015" :question/math-academy-id "q-111955" :question/problem "![](images/05/05173f7d9b4cdf89d4167f71533da6b95942bf6355bc6245fc95fbd7c434440e.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above show the graph of $y=-{x}^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that graph III resembles a straight line. So, we disregard this option.\n\nNow, remember that for $x>0,$ the graph of $y=-{x}^{3}$ decreases very rapidly as we increase $x.$ We say that $y\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ The only graphs that exhibit this decreasing property are I and II.\n\nNow, we need to choose between graphs I and II. To do this, let's evaluate $y=-{x}^{3}$ at some value of $x,$ say $x=0.$ Substituting $x=0$ into the function, we get\n\n$$\ny=-(0)^{3}=0,\n$$\n\nso the correct graph must pass through the point $(0,0).$ Only graph II satisfies this criterion.\n\nTherefore, graph II corresponds to the graph of $y=-{x}^{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40093136-bd98-5ca4-838e-58e47b317950" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Vertical Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02787bb6-13ec-5ee4-8136-0d2743da1062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x+1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526505} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9cd00e-409e-50b0-8cdc-fad4ad3f0443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526568} {:answer/id #uuid "49fca1c1-6a50-548c-9dd1-b7e2aa7647f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526653} {:answer/id #uuid "84aaa720-7c42-558d-afb2-80d78b9c937b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526769} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf60cbe-5d6b-51c3-92ad-654e5175b298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84aaa720-7c42-558d-afb2-80d78b9c937b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526769} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac670fba-dba7-56ca-886b-c347dd341b10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3b4690a-a388-56c8-b51f-66b065fce082" :question/math-academy-id "q-18336" :question/problem "![](images/04/04cb5fcb2ea4013f64d76439a882730455f77908c9e885f52f262efce7bccb58.png)\n\nWhat's the equation of the above curve?" :question/worked-solution "This is the curve $y={x}^{3}$ that's been translated $1$ unit *down*.\n\n![](images/18/1827cffb455aeea03512c208f1cd2914ce669abc62a27dd56cb52c29bf8094c4.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y={x}^{3}\\,-\\,1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f1cf641-888f-576c-b9c3-0bdf62a00fb8" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Horizontal and Vertical Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ccf67de-d8ad-5444-8186-0e2370406a26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x-3)^{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526784} {:answer/id #uuid "b386ad48-3407-54d4-a595-371ba41e6e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x-2)^{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526846} {:answer/id #uuid "c277b7fb-554d-5014-966c-492d07a2246c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x+2)^{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526873} {:answer/id #uuid "da80e664-a2c5-58d1-8a4b-7f8a384f145e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x-2)^{3}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526925} {:answer/id #uuid "e71b0835-f4b3-58d7-a3e6-93fc36e1024d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x+2)^{3}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b386ad48-3407-54d4-a595-371ba41e6e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x-2)^{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526846} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1ac20f8-79b8-5bcf-87a9-d3d6c49f7850" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b8be0e4-6ba2-573c-9c5f-c0fd730c101c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18340" :question/problem "![](images/74/74718361ade9a3a1a5123cbebe26baf2b49a6ae4739b544fe5b41578bd71d038.png)\n\nWhat's the equation of the above curve?" :question/worked-solution "This is the curve $y={x}^{3}$ that's been translated \n\n- $2$ units to the *right*, and\n\n- $2$ units *down*.\n\n![](images/c6/c652e1639e68ecc5f09fccce36ed236e7bad3f99d704e95c40286afa5db66963.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=(x\\,-\\,2)^{3}\\,-\\,2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8acb08f-56b0-5a1b-b503-ba70e1cf88e6" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Horizontal Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12ebbd82-9539-589c-8662-61a518dfc266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-({x}^{3}+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526539} {:answer/id #uuid "31081246-6ab8-58a3-8951-3221cb63fde2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{x}^{3}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526598} {:answer/id #uuid "3db0e161-b46c-5f77-9c15-40063c245921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-(x-3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526619} {:answer/id #uuid "93ad9127-c3a2-5e06-b797-92f348fcca91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{x}^{3}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526791} {:answer/id #uuid "f875181f-1a30-5dcf-b0e9-f6c379281589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-(x+3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f875181f-1a30-5dcf-b0e9-f6c379281589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-(x+3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526994} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3349cb5-9ec8-5ffb-ae15-e2a038997e40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "128afa31-6089-55bb-b4c5-d34347e7a11c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18347" :question/problem "![](images/40/4030ed55caa6900e6927021a1b4819d4fd2157b803fc23ccc05165ba01bd3fce.png)\n\nWhat's the equation of the above curve?" :question/worked-solution "This is the curve $y=-{x}^{3}$ that's been translated $3$ units *left*.\n\n![](images/d9/d933bb153126e39091c73df703facc27e149fb793021eb4b38a5456b76d42bb1.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=-(x\\,+\\,3)^{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115270 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f1cf641-888f-576c-b9c3-0bdf62a00fb8" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Horizontal and Vertical Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a7ff7c-7c86-5b2b-834b-f728e5c1c819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-(x+1)^{3}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526500} {:answer/id #uuid "01cddc3e-8940-559b-aea6-132bf9816888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-(x-2)^{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526504} {:answer/id #uuid "611916a6-5737-5d2a-a9fe-9aeca2444409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x-2)^{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526696} {:answer/id #uuid "79913651-f292-58fd-b075-1bb74738413b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-(x+2)^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526741} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d02359-b9ca-5615-8018-e92f809f1b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-(x-1)^{3}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01cddc3e-8940-559b-aea6-132bf9816888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-(x-2)^{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526504} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d94d905-22ff-5e12-bb42-d1acedbfba1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26a8d25b-e6dd-5460-9414-80558f8bec9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-18349" :question/problem "![](images/46/46d382b4d31818e63f917b8df074a5710e187362fc1aaa125a28245a371564cd.png)\n\nWhat's the equation of the above curve?" :question/worked-solution "This is the curve $y=-{x}^{3}$ that's been translated \n\n- $2$ units to the *right*, and\n\n- $1$ unit *up*.\n\n![](images/4d/4d0840ff427022b8bf23ebd3d36d58bf0e5bbe75d339f139ed86930d53eec09d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=-(x\\,-\\,2)^{3}\\,+\\,1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40093136-bd98-5ca4-838e-58e47b317950" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Vertical Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "983dda4e-6514-5175-bc14-90521fd35347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^3+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "983dda4e-6514-5175-bc14-90521fd35347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^3+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526801} :answer-field/id #uuid "868907ed-371e-58bf-ba87-262f027567a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d93e70df-0d5a-518e-ab33-73b00d22f653" :question/math-academy-id "q-276204" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d20da3acdbbf1f08a5c0713ce2fe0313a345319accfa1b18efbc87f46705faa8.png)\n\nThe graph above is a translation of $y={x}^{3}.$ Identify the equation that generated the graph.\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This is the curve $y={x}^{3}$ that's been translated $6$ units *up*.\n\n![](images/07/078aa5c391829a1544d0f83c51c32e0653312f2b06158200ffc82dd8cd784330.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y={x}^{3}+6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115267 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e509fc70-f78c-5daa-bf55-e23ed6a2b046" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Graph of an Elementary Cubic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d16aa3-4c71-58f6-ba0d-c2d0dbd878a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526549} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0b9457-6e1e-59f5-ac5f-fc8ba9873630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526688} {:answer/id #uuid "64a8da2d-0d35-5cbe-959d-acfa147a54c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526704} {:answer/id #uuid "e04be6cf-2bee-5ebe-9ec6-ecf2e87a6960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526942} {:answer/id #uuid "e5edc2d1-f6a8-56b5-81da-c3d888767579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e04be6cf-2bee-5ebe-9ec6-ecf2e87a6960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526942} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddbcedd3-6d01-50a2-b5d0-e40ab1637157" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f99401c-4f2a-57bb-bccb-f67190e5a3b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-28208" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d341093cf35425a75174a6871d452c38daa0d281cdc2a2b7aaceeca390dee5b.png)\n\nWhich of the following curves is the graph of $y={x}^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, remember that for $x>0,$ the graph of $y={x}^{3}$ increases very rapidly as we increase $x.$ We say that $y\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ The only graphs that exhibit this increasing property are II and IV.\n\nNow, we need to choose between graphs II and IV. To do this, let's evaluate $y={x}^{3}$ at some value of $x,$ say $x=-1.$ Substituting $x=-1$ into the function, we get\n\n$$\ny=(-1)^{3}=-1,\n$$\n\nso the correct graph must pass through the point $(-1,-1).$ Only graph IV satisfies this criterion.\n\nTherefore, graph IV corresponds to the graph of $y={x}^{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115269 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8acb08f-56b0-5a1b-b503-ba70e1cf88e6" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Horizontal Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177cf9c8-743c-55f3-89d3-ac27d197af24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x+1)^{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526551} {:answer/id #uuid "32c1accb-968d-506c-9b58-cc71502f9c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526600} {:answer/id #uuid "67d756da-3470-5853-8f02-5228373158cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526709} {:answer/id #uuid "690957e0-edb8-5952-a9d7-5c49c107cb0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x+1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526713} {:answer/id #uuid "a74b9f0d-f72d-5326-a944-8f4ce593278e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "690957e0-edb8-5952-a9d7-5c49c107cb0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x+1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526713} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f98ffef-14c8-5933-a045-a10b6f9d9b19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92488220-68fc-5f69-b251-46eba62a932c" :question/math-academy-id "q-6639" :question/problem "![](images/b7/b71c0bba1fff92996920e7d62a9e2b33feecd53f24edbbc309799b69e7cc79e2.png)\n\nWhat's the equation of the above curve?" :question/worked-solution "This is the curve $y={x}^{3}$ that's been translated $1$ unit *left*.\n\n![](images/83/839a3c17eebac5a44ab2ddbcbef83c9087429ab9ad6d05f8dd98689d35f356bc.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=(x\\,+\\,1)^{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115268 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40093136-bd98-5ca4-838e-58e47b317950" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing Vertical Translations of Elementary Cubic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choic